+def _lucaryin_auth_dirs() -> list[Path]:
+    """Resolved ``~/.lucaryin/auth`` and ``$LUCARYIN_AUTH_DIR`` (the bridge points
+    every agent at the former): the desktop app's connector tokens
+    (``{connector}.token``, read by bridges) and, since B1, the bridge's own bearer
+    (``bridge.token``, published for readers whose env no longer carries it —
+    hermes-bridge/server.py ``_publish_bridge_bearer_file``, which states the
+    runtime's deny set must cover it). The bridge gate cards a shell touch of
+    either spelling as credential_read; a cron job granted credential_read at
+    creation would still have read the bearer through read_file card-free, so the
+    file tools refuse the whole directory, read and write, at every trust level.
+    Nothing shipped reads it through them: the Google and Plaid skills use a
